From db225239dc87f234ee2d8b58c991712afbce9a2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:14:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.6.2: imported Pokemon get three PP Ups and true
 maximum PP

Every Pokemon built from a Showdown paste used to get a flat PP value (35 on
the Gen 3 side, 40 on the Gen 4 side) and no PP Ups, on the assumption that the
game clamps PP on use. In battle that reads as moves that are not PP maxed:
Thunderbolt at 15 instead of 24, Earthquake at 10 instead of 16.

Built Pokemon now carry three PP Ups on every filled move slot and current PP
at the real maximum for that move (base + 3 * base / 5, the games' own
formula). An empty slot carries neither, the way the games leave it.

The base PP tables are per generation, because some moves changed between
them (Giga Drain 5 in Gen 3 and 10 in Gen 4, Recover 20 and 10). Each table
was extracted by script and compared entry by entry against a second,
independent source; both pairs agree on every id (355 Gen 3 ids, 468 Gen 4
ids), and every id was aligned against the bundled name to id maps.

 - Gen3Data::MoveBasePp / MoveMaxPp (C++), used by MonFactory. This is the
   path behind the desktop Team Editor and Submit Team for both players on
   every platform.
 - Gen3MovePp.kt, used by the Android Team Editor's MonFactory.
 - Gen4MovePp.kt, used by Bk4Factory and by the PBR editor when a move is
   changed. A slot whose move did not change keeps its PP and PP Ups, since
   they may come from the player's own save.

Pokemon taken from a player's own save ("Use my save", imported saves) are not
touched. A team that was built before this version keeps its old PP until it
is imported again.
